# Which built image every NAME resolves to. One file, so a version bump is one edit.
#
# The problem this exists to stop: nothing pointed at an image by role, so every consumer spelled
# a version. 169 campaign .env files still say optarena-amd-mi300-v4 and canon_column.sh says v5,
# which is not a decision anyone made -- it is where each file happened to stop being edited. A
# results table then cites an EDF name that means a different image depending on when it was run.
#
# So: consumers name LATEST, this file says what latest is, and promotion is a one-line change
# here followed by install_edfs.sh. A run that must stay pinned to one build names the version
# explicitly instead -- that is what pinning is for, and it is still available.
#
# The DIGEST remains the identity of a build. LATEST is a convenience for launching, never the
# thing a results table quotes; build.sh writes <sqsh>.digest for that.

# ONE VERSION PER ROLE. Every name here is unversioned and every rebuild replaces it, so there is
# never a v2 and a v8 to reconcile: the .sqsh basename says which image it is and the .digest says
# which build. A build writes <role>-candidate.sqsh and build.sbatch refuses to write over an image
# an EDF mounts, so promotion is verify-then-rename and a running arm never reads a half-written
# squashfs.
#
# What this gives up, deliberately: there is no version to pin a run to. A results table cites the
# DIGEST, which was always the identity anyway -- a moving tag over two different images is what
# made citing one meaningless.

# Judge + agent. ONE image serves both the CPU arms and the GPU arms -- there is no separate CPU
# build, and the GPU entries below are inference engines, not a second judge image.
JUDGE_AGENT_AMD_SQSH="optarena-ce-amd-mi300.sqsh"
JUDGE_AGENT_AMD_EDF_LATEST="optarena-amd-mi300-latest"
JUDGE_AGENT_AMD_TEMPLATE="judge-agent-amd/edf.toml.example"

# Inference, the three engines campaigns mount: sglang serves qwen38 and kimi (130 arms), vllm
# 0.23.0 serves oss120b because its mxfp4 path is what 0.23.0 has (68 arms), vllm 0.27.1 keeps a
# separate 12 (see below).
#
# All three now name an image this repo builds from a single Dockerfile. Until 2026-09-08 they
# named upstream pulls produced by the multi-phase chain in inference/build/, and what
# sglang/Dockerfile, vllm/Dockerfile and vllm-0271/Dockerfile build had never been promoted into
# service. That is why the sglang arms still carried PYTHONPATH=${SCRATCH}/pyprefix for cupy and
# flydsl: the served image did not have them. The pulls also carried a squashfs sha256 and no
# .digest, so publishing one published something the repo could not rebuild.
#
# The already-installed rocm723-vllm-* EDFs still resolve to those pulls, so a run that must not
# move can name one instead of -latest. install_edfs.sh does not re-render them.
INFERENCE_SGLANG_SQSH="${INFERENCE_SGLANG_SQSH:-optarena-sglang.sqsh}"
INFERENCE_SGLANG_EDF="sglang-rocm-mi30x"
INFERENCE_SGLANG_EDF_LATEST="sglang-latest"
INFERENCE_SGLANG_TEMPLATE="sglang/edf.toml.example"
INFERENCE_VLLM_SQSH="${INFERENCE_VLLM_SQSH:-optarena-vllm.sqsh}"
INFERENCE_VLLM_EDF="rocm723-vllm-0.23.0-pytorch211-ofi"
INFERENCE_VLLM_EDF_LATEST="vllm-latest"
INFERENCE_VLLM_TEMPLATE="vllm/edf.toml.example"

# vLLM 0.27.1 keeps its OWN latest. Folding its arms into vllm-latest would move them from 0.27.1
# to 0.23.0 -- a different engine, not a newer build of the same one, and the two are kept apart
# deliberately because oss120b needs 0.23.0's mxfp4 path.
INFERENCE_VLLM_0271_SQSH="${INFERENCE_VLLM_0271_SQSH:-optarena-vllm-0271.sqsh}"
INFERENCE_VLLM_0271_EDF_LATEST="vllm-0271-latest"
INFERENCE_VLLM_0271_TEMPLATE="vllm-0271/edf.toml.example"

# PROMOTION: build to <role>-candidate.sqsh, run verify_image.sbatch on it, rename it over the
# live name above, then re-run install_edfs.sh with ALLOW_REPOINT=1. The rename is safe while arms
# are running -- a mounted squashfs is held by its inode, so a job that already started keeps
# reading the bytes it opened and only new jobs see the new image.
#
# Keep the .digest and .sha256 sidecars with the rename. They are the only record of WHICH build a
# name currently holds, and with one version per role there is nothing else to tell two apart.

# Registry: ONE repository for every image -- https://hub.docker.com/r/spcleth/hpcagent-bench
#
# The tag is the .sqsh basename minus the optarena- prefix, so it names the ROLE -- ce-amd-mi300,
# sglang, vllm, vllm-0271 -- and a published tag cannot drift from the file it was built from.
# These tags MOVE, one per role, exactly like the .sqsh they mirror. push_image.sh publishes a
# sha-<digest> tag alongside each: cite that, never the moving one.
REGISTRY_REPO="${REGISTRY_REPO:-docker.io/spcleth/hpcagent-bench}"
sqsh_tag() { local b="${1##*/}"; b="${b%.sqsh}"; printf '%s' "${b#optarena-}"; }
JUDGE_AGENT_AMD_REPO="${REGISTRY_REPO}"
INFERENCE_SGLANG_REPO="${REGISTRY_REPO}"
INFERENCE_VLLM_REPO="${REGISTRY_REPO}"
INFERENCE_VLLM_0271_REPO="${REGISTRY_REPO}"
JUDGE_AGENT_AMD_TAG="$(sqsh_tag "${JUDGE_AGENT_AMD_SQSH}")"
INFERENCE_SGLANG_TAG="$(sqsh_tag "${INFERENCE_SGLANG_SQSH}")"
INFERENCE_VLLM_TAG="$(sqsh_tag "${INFERENCE_VLLM_SQSH}")"
INFERENCE_VLLM_0271_TAG="$(sqsh_tag "${INFERENCE_VLLM_0271_SQSH}")"
